WEBVTT

00:23.480 --> 00:25.110
Sorry for the wait!

00:26.650 --> 00:29.120
They were out of chocolate, but vanilla's okay, right?

00:29.790 --> 00:33.020
Yeah, whichever. It doesn't matter.

00:33.860 --> 00:35.450
You think so?

00:35.660 --> 00:38.530
I like green tea, but they don't have that here.

00:39.400 --> 00:40.430
Did you go swimming?

00:40.430 --> 00:41.420
Not yet.

00:41.500 --> 00:43.200
We're at the ocean.

00:43.270 --> 00:44.500
I will, eventually.

00:44.500 --> 00:46.470
Oh, wanna play with the beach ball?

00:47.140 --> 00:48.160
That's okay.

00:49.670 --> 00:51.140
Y-yeah, you're right.

00:51.210 --> 00:54.010
We're in high school, beach ball is too kiddy for us.

00:58.880 --> 01:00.850
<i>What's the matter with you, Kazuki?</i>

01:01.090 --> 01:02.290
<i>You've been acting weird...</i>

01:02.290 --> 01:04.420
<i>... ever since the last</i> <i>exhibition and spot sale.</i>

01:12.800 --> 01:16.360
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:16.900 --> 01:20.010
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:20.010 --> 01:23.570
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

01:23.810 --> 01:26.840
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:27.110 --> 01:30.750
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

01:30.750 --> 01:34.320
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

01:34.320 --> 01:37.690
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

01:37.890 --> 01:41.380
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

01:41.490 --> 01:44.860
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

01:45.060 --> 01:48.470
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

01:48.630 --> 01:53.040
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

01:53.270 --> 01:56.170
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

01:56.470 --> 02:02.410
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

02:02.750 --> 02:09.480
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

02:10.120 --> 02:14.080
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

02:14.160 --> 02:17.300
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

02:17.300 --> 02:21.070
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:21.070 --> 02:24.330
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

02:24.400 --> 02:28.170
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

02:28.510 --> 02:31.640
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

02:31.640 --> 02:35.240
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:35.410 --> 02:38.350
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:41.350 --> 02:48.160
AT

02:41.350 --> 02:48.160
THE

02:41.350 --> 02:48.160
SEASHORE...

02:56.870 --> 03:00.460
Inner Tubes

02:56.870 --> 03:00.460
Rubber Boats

03:00.670 --> 03:04.340
Say, you think we should've gone to a bigger swimming area?

03:04.710 --> 03:06.880
It's the same, no matter where we go.

03:06.880 --> 03:08.610
Y-yeah, you're right.

03:10.050 --> 03:12.450
<i>Kazuki, is it still bothering you?</i>

03:18.460 --> 03:19.690
Please take care of it, then.

03:19.690 --> 03:21.750
All right, thank you very much!

03:29.800 --> 03:31.600
How long're you gonna stay like that?

03:31.740 --> 03:33.970
The delivery service's gonna close if you don't hurry up.

03:34.310 --> 03:36.400
Or are ya plannin' on takin' it back with you?

03:37.010 --> 03:38.310
Yeah.

03:40.750 --> 03:42.110
Just this one?

03:42.480 --> 03:43.210
It'll be 1,200 yen.

03:43.820 --> 03:46.250
Oh, it's over! It's over!

03:46.720 --> 03:49.810
Come on, let's go to karaoke or somethin' and celebrate!

03:50.390 --> 03:52.520
Very well! I see you do not know...

03:52.520 --> 03:54.720
...that I am called the Great
Demon King of anime karaoke!

03:55.790 --> 03:57.130
I challenge you!

03:57.130 --> 03:58.100
Sure!

03:58.260 --> 03:59.660
You'll come, too, right?

03:59.730 --> 04:01.530
What? Me?

04:01.930 --> 04:04.640
Yeah, you came all this way to the exhibition and spot sale that you hate...

04:04.640 --> 04:06.370
...just to see Kazuki, after all.

04:06.440 --> 04:08.460
N-no, I don't really...

04:09.040 --> 04:10.980
You don't hafta hide it.

04:11.240 --> 04:12.870
I'm not hiding anything!

04:13.010 --> 04:14.840
Well, whatever. Come on, let's go.

04:14.950 --> 04:16.210
W-wait...

04:16.550 --> 04:18.380
I'll pass.

04:18.550 --> 04:19.280
What?

04:19.280 --> 04:21.780
What's the matter? You look glum.

04:22.590 --> 04:25.250
Oh, I get it. It's 'cause your books didn't sell, isn't it?

04:27.560 --> 04:29.550
It's nothin' to worry about.

04:29.630 --> 04:31.530
I was like that, too, at the beginnin'.

04:31.960 --> 04:34.230
I went about it the wrong way to gain popularity and failed miserably.

04:34.230 --> 04:37.730
I sadly ended up sendin' my remainin' stock to the recycler's.

04:37.940 --> 04:41.400
Hey, country panda! What did you do with your leftover books?!

04:41.470 --> 04:42.500
E-Eimi...

04:42.570 --> 04:46.170
You probably sent a whole stack of them back by cat-cat delivery, right?

04:46.980 --> 04:48.310
Leftover panda!

04:48.380 --> 04:51.710
Having leftover at a huge event like this is just super-uncool!

04:51.820 --> 04:54.820
Super-embarrassing!

04:52.320 --> 04:54.350
Hey, quit it, Eimi!

04:54.550 --> 04:55.840
Eimi!

04:56.090 --> 04:57.560
Wh-what?

05:00.590 --> 05:03.690
It really is super-uncool.

05:06.560 --> 05:07.930
Oh, Kazuki!

05:08.770 --> 05:10.060
My sister!

05:13.870 --> 05:14.960
Taishi?

05:15.040 --> 05:16.230
My sister.

05:18.080 --> 05:21.210
You should listen to my alluring karaoke at least once!

05:21.310 --> 05:25.110
Shimon or Sasaki or
Kageyama! I can sing them all!

05:25.780 --> 05:28.910
Listen! Listen and worship me!

05:33.120 --> 05:34.420
Kazuki!

05:40.400 --> 05:42.030
Hey, come over here!

05:42.130 --> 05:43.930
There's a jellyfish! Jellyfish!

05:44.070 --> 05:45.730
No, it's dangerous!

05:45.970 --> 05:48.510
You gotta have surgery if you get stung!

05:47.340 --> 05:49.060
Looks like they're having fun.

05:49.640 --> 05:52.580
Watching them sort of makes me want to swim now.

05:53.510 --> 05:55.740
Do you think it'll hurt if I get stung by a jellyfish?

05:56.510 --> 05:57.950
I haven't been to the ocean in a while.

05:57.950 --> 05:59.920
What'll I do if I pull a muscle in my leg?

06:01.820 --> 06:02.950
Would you rescue me?

06:23.470 --> 06:24.810
Damn it!

06:27.010 --> 06:28.410
Why?

06:29.080 --> 06:30.340
Why?!

06:35.250 --> 06:37.090
Why...

06:38.860 --> 06:40.850
Kazuki, there's a letter for you.

06:41.130 --> 06:42.290
Leave it there.

06:42.290 --> 06:44.420
You should study sometime, too.

06:53.270 --> 06:54.010
Mr. Kazuki Sendou

06:54.010 --> 06:56.060
Ikumi Tachikawa

06:54.510 --> 06:56.060
Miss Tachikawa!

06:56.840 --> 06:58.070
She bought one!

07:09.450 --> 07:14.150
"I was not very impressed with the latest issue."

07:23.100 --> 07:24.900
Kazuki!

07:33.080 --> 07:36.210
The water's a little cold, but it's nice since it isn't crowded.

07:36.510 --> 07:38.280
What? Oh.

07:49.360 --> 07:51.630
Flavored Ice

08:03.270 --> 08:05.240
Flavored Ice

08:06.440 --> 08:07.710
Say, Kazuki,

08:07.710 --> 08:10.980
the food here at this beach house isn't that great, is it?

08:11.980 --> 08:13.250
This is probably normal.

08:14.790 --> 08:15.620
But you know...

08:16.120 --> 08:17.950
If you don't like it, just leave it.

08:22.730 --> 08:24.590
<i>We have a hurricane warning.</i>

08:25.430 --> 08:29.730
<i>Due to the effects of Hurricane</i> <i>#1 1, which turned east yesterday,</i>

08:29.930 --> 08:33.670
<i>a warning for strong winds, waves,</i> <i>high seas, and heavy rain...</i>

08:30.800 --> 08:32.800
Do you think they'll

08:30.800 --> 08:32.800
prohibit swimming again?

08:32.800 --> 08:35.140
It's after the Bon Festival,

08:32.800 --> 08:35.140
it can't be helped.

08:34.340 --> 08:36.710
<i>... has been issued for the Kantou Region.</i>

08:36.340 --> 08:39.230
Did you hear that?

08:36.710 --> 08:39.230
<i>Please listen for further</i> <i>hurricane warnings.</i>

08:39.310 --> 08:40.470
The bus...

08:40.550 --> 08:41.710
What?

08:42.710 --> 08:45.680
The bus service might stop if we don't hurry home.

08:46.150 --> 08:49.250
It'll be okay. The hurricane's still far away.

08:50.690 --> 08:51.750
If...

08:52.260 --> 08:55.120
If the bus service does stop, what would you do?

08:55.860 --> 08:57.350
Thanks for the food.

09:06.040 --> 09:08.400
What?! A guy?!

09:12.910 --> 09:14.610
That's not what I meant.

09:14.610 --> 09:17.280
So, like, I'm talking about my friend from middle school.

09:17.850 --> 09:20.550
Oh, you scared me there for a sec.

09:21.020 --> 09:23.750
I thought maybe you'd gotten ahead of us.

09:23.920 --> 09:25.180
Sorry about that.

09:25.720 --> 09:29.220
So, is that guy your friend's boyfriend?

09:29.630 --> 09:30.530
Boyfriend?

09:30.530 --> 09:34.330
Yeah, yeah, boyfriend, darling, lover, also known as a steady.

09:34.400 --> 09:36.960
I-I don't think it's anything like that, but...

09:41.210 --> 09:45.910
Anyway, my friend's, well, we'll call him her boyfriend.

09:46.210 --> 09:49.040
He seems to have had a bad experience with his hobby recently.

09:49.550 --> 09:50.780
Like how?

09:50.850 --> 09:54.840
He was at this event thing, but
I guess it didn't go too well.

09:54.990 --> 09:56.550
Oh, like a concert or something?

09:57.020 --> 09:58.260
Something like that.

09:58.260 --> 10:00.450
And she tries to get him to go out and have fun,

10:00.530 --> 10:02.320
but he just doesn't seem to get into it.

10:03.660 --> 10:04.820
Toss him.

10:05.060 --> 10:06.200
What?

10:06.200 --> 10:08.630
If he's the kind of guy that takes it out on his girlfriend...

10:08.630 --> 10:10.500
...just because some event didn't work out...

10:10.700 --> 10:12.570
She's got a point. He sounds like a loser.

10:12.840 --> 10:15.810
Oh, but it's not that he's taking it out on her or anything.

10:16.010 --> 10:19.740
But normally, don't you think he should care more about his girlfriend?

10:19.940 --> 10:21.310
Yeah, yeah.

10:21.480 --> 10:23.880
You can try events over and over again,

10:24.020 --> 10:26.280
but you only have one girlfriend in the world.

10:26.450 --> 10:28.780
Wow, Reina, you sound so serious!

10:29.050 --> 10:30.250
Shut up!

10:30.250 --> 10:33.280
Why don't you get back together with your old boyfriend already?

10:33.490 --> 10:34.990
That guy is scum.

10:34.990 --> 10:36.460
For real?

10:35.660 --> 10:37.060
Way real.

10:36.460 --> 10:38.290
Oh come on, just forgive him.

10:52.380 --> 10:54.210
It's getting choppy out there.

10:55.380 --> 10:56.610
Yeah.

10:56.680 --> 10:57.880
What do you want to do?

10:57.880 --> 10:59.040
Whatever.

10:59.220 --> 11:00.710
What do you mean, whatever?

11:01.420 --> 11:02.180
Kazuki!

11:03.750 --> 11:06.450
I'm sorry, I forgot my purse!

11:06.890 --> 11:08.420
Go on back without me!

11:17.270 --> 11:19.240
I'm so glad I noticed it right away.

11:33.620 --> 11:37.080
Beach House

11:55.240 --> 11:57.110
Hey, where are you from?

11:57.480 --> 11:59.140
No, I'm, um...

11:59.640 --> 12:01.700
They're gonna prohibit swimming real soon.

12:02.250 --> 12:04.410
Come to our car and let's go have some fun.

12:04.620 --> 12:06.410
I know the area pretty good.

12:06.650 --> 12:07.620
I'm with a friend...

12:08.050 --> 12:11.080
Hey, that sounds good.
Get your friend to come along, too.

12:11.260 --> 12:14.280
Yeah, for real. It'll be a lot more fun than the ocean.

12:14.790 --> 12:15.850
But...

12:15.990 --> 12:17.960
Oh, Kazuki!

12:18.530 --> 12:20.430
Damn, she's got a boyfriend?

12:20.530 --> 12:22.230
Say that first, sheesh.

12:25.670 --> 12:27.300
Did you come to save me?

12:27.510 --> 12:28.630
From what?

12:28.710 --> 12:30.900
They were hitting on me.
You saw it, didn't you?

12:33.680 --> 12:35.110
Hey, Kazuki?

12:37.620 --> 12:39.580
You don't care if they were hitting on me?

12:39.650 --> 12:40.710
Free choice.

12:40.790 --> 12:42.290
What do you mean?

12:41.550 --> 12:43.050
It's your choice.

12:43.720 --> 12:46.020
More importantly, over there...

12:47.360 --> 12:49.380
<i>The waves have become stronger,</i>

12:49.490 --> 12:52.990
<i>so swimming will now be</i> <i>prohibited at this beach.</i>

12:53.160 --> 12:55.690
<i>If you are still in the ocean,</i> <i>please come ashore immediately.</i>

12:56.530 --> 12:57.740
<i>I repeat...</i>

12:57.740 --> 12:59.900
<i>The waves have become stronger,</i>

12:57.740 --> 12:59.100
Excuse me.

12:59.970 --> 13:03.130
<i>so swimming will now be</i> <i>prohibited at this beach.</i>

13:03.410 --> 13:05.480
It looks like it might rain.

13:03.610 --> 13:06.640
<i>If you are still in the ocean,</i> <i>please come ashore immediately.</i>

13:07.110 --> 13:08.600
What should we do?

13:17.460 --> 13:18.580
Hello, there!

13:18.690 --> 13:20.090
Aren't you home?

13:20.190 --> 13:21.850
I am coming in!

13:23.690 --> 13:28.100
Ah, you are here after all, my brother!

13:29.170 --> 13:30.600
Is that a game?

13:31.600 --> 13:33.970
Oh, it's the one where you collect the monsters.

13:34.370 --> 13:36.270
Is that the source for your next comic?

13:37.610 --> 13:39.630
Collecting monsters is all well and good, but...

13:40.180 --> 13:42.340
My brother, behold!

13:42.450 --> 13:45.380
The numerous spoils of war that I got at Comi-Pa!

13:45.480 --> 13:47.280
Truly, a fortune to bequeath to the future!

13:47.420 --> 13:51.720
Or a map to the legendary Treasure
Island, where the treasures are buried!

13:54.460 --> 13:56.090
They are all currently explosively popular ones,

13:56.160 --> 13:58.430
which I obtained from the wall-space groups!

13:59.230 --> 14:01.360
Gag! Eimi's is in there, too!

14:01.570 --> 14:04.190
Never mind that! Popular sellers equal good quality!

14:04.340 --> 14:08.430
Comrade Kazuki, summer break is your time to do research.

14:08.670 --> 14:10.470
Using this failure as a springboard,

14:10.570 --> 14:15.410
you and I will work out an even more advanced plan for world conquest!

14:18.220 --> 14:19.550
Failure, huh?

14:20.680 --> 14:24.380
Yeah, it was a failure, wasn't it?

14:25.520 --> 14:27.010
Do not let it bother you!

14:27.090 --> 14:30.150
In a sense, this was a predictable result.

14:30.660 --> 14:32.200
I told you too, remember?

14:32.200 --> 14:35.260
I got too wrapped up about makin' a seller at the beginnin' and failed.

14:35.770 --> 14:39.230
However, you could not have known that without actually experiencing it!

14:39.400 --> 14:42.770
That is exactly why I did not stop you this time.

14:43.040 --> 14:46.070
Failure is the mother of success.

14:46.540 --> 14:47.600
Taishi...

14:49.180 --> 14:51.740
You're always like that.

14:52.720 --> 14:53.450
Why?

14:54.320 --> 14:57.290
You knew it beforehand.
It's exactly as you had calculated it.

14:57.390 --> 14:59.550
Everything is going your way.

14:59.760 --> 15:02.890
But you know, it's easy to say that after the fact.

15:03.690 --> 15:07.530
No! What is the matter, my brother?!

15:08.430 --> 15:10.490
You dragged me off to that exhibition and spot sale!

15:10.570 --> 15:12.430
You made me do that book!

15:12.700 --> 15:15.100
Think about how I feel for once!

15:16.070 --> 15:18.300
Wait! Wait just a minute,
Comrade Kazuki!

15:18.640 --> 15:19.840
Stop!

15:21.080 --> 15:23.070
It's better if you leave him alone for now.

15:23.550 --> 15:24.850
But...

15:25.450 --> 15:27.120
Well, sorry to have bothered you.

15:27.120 --> 15:29.520
Wait, my sister!

15:28.320 --> 15:29.950
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

15:30.090 --> 15:31.020
Sister!

15:32.060 --> 15:33.850
I know what you're tryin' to say,

15:35.430 --> 15:36.550
but you know,

15:37.130 --> 15:39.760
you were havin' all that fun doin' it, too.

15:41.030 --> 15:43.390
W-wait! Uh...

15:41.030 --> 15:42.370
See ya.

15:51.610 --> 15:52.840
Kazuki.

15:53.840 --> 15:55.510
Hey, Kazuki!

15:55.610 --> 15:56.510
What?

15:56.580 --> 15:58.570
So, what are we going to do after this?

15:58.980 --> 16:00.320
After this?

16:00.420 --> 16:01.910
It's only 2 o'clock!

16:02.020 --> 16:02.990
Oh...

16:02.990 --> 16:05.390
You wanna go back early and go see a movie or something?

16:05.390 --> 16:06.760
A movie, huh?

16:06.960 --> 16:08.520
Or go to an arcade, maybe?

16:09.590 --> 16:11.820
All right, then! Just for today,
I'll keep you company...

16:11.960 --> 16:15.020
...wherever you want to go, even if it's to an art supply store!

16:15.930 --> 16:18.630
Oh, you wanna go to that doujinshi shop we went to that time?

16:18.740 --> 16:20.000
You should have fun there...

16:20.670 --> 16:21.900
Doujinshi?

16:22.140 --> 16:24.900
Wow, I guess you didn't hate it then.

16:26.310 --> 16:28.780
But it doesn't matter anymore.

16:32.620 --> 16:33.950
It doesn't matter.

16:45.000 --> 16:46.120
Jerk.

16:53.970 --> 16:54.900
Jerk.

16:55.440 --> 16:57.740
Jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk!

16:59.010 --> 16:59.530
Hey...

16:59.910 --> 17:01.970
Kazuki, you jerk! You big jerk!

17:02.150 --> 17:03.580
See if I care anymore!

17:04.010 --> 17:05.350
Hey!

17:12.260 --> 17:13.880
A jerk, huh?

17:18.460 --> 17:21.020
It's really starting to rain!

17:21.200 --> 17:22.670
This sucks.

17:23.970 --> 17:26.600
You've gotta be kidding me, sheesh.

17:31.610 --> 17:32.800
Jerk...

17:41.720 --> 17:46.020
Hey, why are you so spaced out?

17:46.390 --> 17:47.980
What was that about?

17:48.390 --> 17:51.620
You weren't looking sharp, so I just gave you a heads up, that's all.

17:52.600 --> 17:57.260
Wow, I guess you're helping out around the house during summer break.

17:57.840 --> 17:59.330
I'm impressed.

17:59.470 --> 18:01.410
My mom asked me to.

18:01.570 --> 18:03.200
So, what do you want?

18:03.670 --> 18:06.710
Y-you're probably always shut away in your room...

18:06.710 --> 18:08.650
...with the air conditioner on, right?

18:09.510 --> 18:10.780
I guess.

18:11.020 --> 18:13.250
You should go out to play once in a while.

18:13.480 --> 18:16.650
Or you'll turn all soft, like melting ice cream.

18:16.790 --> 18:18.310
Well, excuse me.

18:19.090 --> 18:20.220
A reward!

18:21.390 --> 18:23.730
Because you're being good and helping out around the house.

18:25.360 --> 18:26.090
So?

18:26.460 --> 18:28.590
I'll take you to the ocean!

18:31.500 --> 18:32.800
Don't want to?

18:33.270 --> 18:35.900
The ocean after the Bon Festival, huh?

18:36.670 --> 18:39.010
It's okay if you don't want to.

18:39.180 --> 18:40.840
I've got time to kill anyway.

18:40.940 --> 18:41.810
You sure?!

18:42.250 --> 18:44.810
Well, I don't really mind.

18:45.150 --> 18:47.020
All right!

18:47.890 --> 18:49.050
Where should we go?

18:49.050 --> 18:52.650
Enoshima? Chigasaki?
Isago? Or maybe Chiba?

18:54.090 --> 18:55.650
I don't care. Wherever.

18:55.890 --> 18:58.190
Okay, well, in that case...

19:13.040 --> 19:14.310
<i>Jerk.</i>

19:15.280 --> 19:17.650
<i>I'm such an idiot.</i>

19:18.850 --> 19:20.480
<i>I get all happy by myself...</i>

19:20.980 --> 19:22.650
<i>...and get all excited by myself,</i>

19:23.350 --> 19:25.250
<i>and keep talking all by myself...</i>

19:28.760 --> 19:32.220
Parasols

20:07.460 --> 20:17.240
Beach House

20:22.480 --> 20:25.040
Suiwa Beach

20:29.090 --> 20:33.180
Beach House

22:20.630 --> 22:24.840
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.840 --> 22:29.330
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:29.470 --> 22:33.880
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:34.040 --> 22:37.950
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:37.950 --> 22:42.050
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:42.050 --> 22:46.320
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:46.490 --> 22:50.930
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:51.060 --> 22:55.070
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:55.070 --> 22:58.640
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:58.640 --> 23:03.540
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:03.710 --> 23:07.210
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:07.210 --> 23:12.650
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:13.720 --> 23:18.160
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:18.160 --> 23:22.190
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:22.190 --> 23:26.730
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:26.730 --> 23:35.660
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:56.360 --> 24:20.580
PREVIEW

24:01.300 --> 24:03.670
Comrade Kazuki, do not get so depressed.

24:03.670 --> 24:05.300
You'll get your chance after that tight spot.

24:05.300 --> 24:06.440
We're just getting started.

24:06.440 --> 24:09.210
Now, let us move forward once again,

24:09.210 --> 24:10.910
so that you may become the emperor of the doujinshi world!

24:10.910 --> 24:12.210
Hey, who are you talkin' to?

24:12.210 --> 24:14.040
Oh? Where is my brother?

24:14.040 --> 24:15.110
I dunno.

24:14.680 --> 24:18.580
Hey! Where have you gone, my brother?!

24:19.320 --> 24:22.190
So, the next episode is "The Unforgettable Dream."

24:21.150 --> 24:26.660
NEXT TIME

24:21.150 --> 24:26.660
<i>THE UNFORGETTABLE</i>

24:21.150 --> 24:26.660
<i>D R E AM</i>

24:22.190 --> 24:24.690
Everyone, watch it together!
